OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788802432
OL,1,Vk4                               G4/20
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGCISKEI FORCES OPEN FIRE
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGON ANC SUPPORTERS
OL,4,D
OL,5, Security forces in the black homeland
OL,6, of Ciskei in South Africa have opened
OL,7, fire on ANC supporters staging a
OL,8, protest against Ciskei's leadership.
OL,10,FA South African official said at least
OL,11,F23 people were killed and 147 injured
OL,12,Fas troops fired on the demonstrators
OL,13,Ffor five minutes.
OL,15,FThe troops opened fire as the AMC march
OL,16,Fwas at a stadium just outside Bisho,
OL,17,Fcapital of Ciskei.
OL,19,FA BBC correspondent said rifle grenades
OL,20,Flanded among the crowd cowering under
OL,21,Fthe hail of live ammunition.
OL,23,D]FFromG07-09-92F  teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11805
SC,0005
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788802432
OL,1,Vk4                               G5/20
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGS AFRICA "NOT INVOLVED
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGIN CISKEI SHOOTINGS"
OL,4,D
OL,5, President de Klerk has said he regrets
OL,6, the murder of ANC protesters in the
OL,7, black homeland of Ciskei, but he said
OL,8, South African forces were not involved.
OL,10,FHe has agreed, however, to deploy a
OL,11,Fcompany of South African troops in
OL,12,FCiskei to prevent further violence.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FThe African National Congress said
OL,15,FCiskei leader Oupa Gqozo and President
OL,16,Fde Klerk were both to blame and the
OL,17,FANC would not respond meekly.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FForeign Secretary Douglas Hurd said
OL,20,Fthat the ramifications of Ciskei would
OL,21,Fhinder the South Adrican peace process.
OL,23,D]FFromG07-09-92F  teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11806
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788802432
OL,1,Vk4                               G6/20
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGMAJOR BACKS
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGMAASTRICHT
OL,4,D
OL,5, Prime Minister John Major has said a
OL,6, French "non" would kill the Maastricht
OL,7, treaty on EC union.
OL,8,F
OL,9,FBut he told a London conference on
OL,10,Fthe future of Europe that the treaty
OL,11,Fdeserved approval.
OL,12,F
OL,13,F"Overall the Maastricht treaty is good
OL,14,Ffor Britain and is good for Europe," Mr
OL,15,FMajor said.
OL,16,F
OL,17,FHe said failure to endorse the treaty
OL,18,Fcould lead to economic and financial
OL,19,Fdisarray. It could also damage chances
OL,20,Feast European countries joining the EC.
OL,21,F
OL,22,D]F This Ceefax page is fromG07-09-92
OL,23,D] FMuch more at: teletextarchive.com
