CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788802432
OL,1,Vk4                              G10/20
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGLABOUR CALLS FOR
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGG7 SUMMIT ON ECONOMY
OL,4,D
OL,5, Labour has called for the top
OL,6, industrialised nations to hold a summit
OL,7, to coordinate economic policies.
OL,9,FShadow Chancellor Gordon Brown said
OL,10,Faction at world level was needed to end
OL,11,Finstability. The old ideology of "do
OL,12,Fnothing" government had failed, he said
OL,13,F
OL,14,FHe said the Group of Seven should
OL,15,Fcreate a permanent administration to
OL,16,Fcoordinate economic policy and maintain
OL,17,Fstable exchange rates.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FThe organisation should be expanded to
OL,20,Finclude east European nations, he said.
OL,21,F
OL,23,D]FFromG07-09-92F  teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
